Job Description
Job Title: User Experience Design Specialist (Multiple Positions Available)
Location: 601 108th Avenue NE, Suite 1000, Bellevue, WA 98004
Ariba, Inc. seeks a User Experience Design Specialist (multiple positions available) at our Bellevue, WA location to create, evaluate, and modify prototypes to support evolving software application development.
Assist in developing design concept and implementation, providing input on user design considerations. Understand our business requirements and any technical limitations. Responsible for conceiving and conducting interviews and surveys, and translating them into sitemaps, user flows, customer journey maps, wireframes, mockups, and prototypes. Design the overall functionality of the product, and to ensure great user experience, in accordance with user testing. Translate concepts into user flows, wireframes, mockups, and prototypes that lead to intuitive user experiences. Facilitate the client’s product vision by researching conceiving, sketching, prototyping, and user-testing experience for digital products. Design and deliver wireframes, user stories, user journeys, and mockups optimized for a wide range of devices and interfaces. Make strategic design and user-experience decisions related to core, and new, functions and features. Take a user-centered design approach and rapidly test and iterate your designs. Communicate design processes, ideas, and solutions to teams and clients. Collaborate and communicate closely with teams and other stakeholders via a distributed model, to regularly deliver design solutions for approval.
Qualifications
Bachelor’s degree or foreign equivalent in Human Computer Interaction, Computer Science, Information Systems, Information Science, or a related field of study and five (5) years of progressive post-baccalaureate experience in the job offered or related occupation. Alternatively, a Master’s degree or foreign equivalent in Human Computer Interaction, Computer Science, Information Systems, Information Science, or a related field of study and three (3) years of experience in the job offered or related occupation.
Qualifications/Skills and Competencies Experience:
Experience must include three (3) years involving each of the following:
Utilizing, customizing, and building analytical user dashboards using business intelligence software including Microsoft Power BI;
Software development kits including UI5 for front-end or back-end technologies;
Creating reusable Figma components for use across enterprise UX teams;
Leading end-to-end projects from requirements to delivery, including aligning cross-functional teams and driving design decisions;
Building interactive prototypes in Figma to support leadership presentation, storytelling, stakeholder alignment, and usability testing;
Designing enterprise widgets, complex procurement flows, and taxonomy management tools;
Building and enhancing admin or power user interfaces;
Designing interfaces to visualize and evaluate machine learning outputs; and
Defining cross-product UX patterns and establishing guidelines for AI/ML features and workflows.
This position is eligible for the Employee Referral Program subject to the eligibility criteria outlined in the SAP Internal Employee Referral Policy .
